if Stargate returns or should I say when  Stargate returns will it really be a  problem that Brad Wright isn't in charge  welcome to Sidetrack your Sci-Fi TV and  movie channel  [Music]  so we have had a lot of discussions on  this channel about the potential of a  new Stargate series or even potentially  a Stargate movie and a lot of those  discussions have been centered around  the very fact that Brad Wright  potentially isn't going to be in charge  of Stargate anymore we've known for a  pretty long time now that the  possibility of Brad Wright not being  involved in Stargate was on the cards  but now it's all but confirmed but is  this really an issue recently we did a  live stream on Star Trek where we  discussed this very possibility the  question was asked if Stargate returned  or rather when it returned would we care  that Brad Wright wasn't involved  and the answer for me personally is no  now before you get into the comments and  you rip into me for this I do have some  very good reasons why I think this and I  feel like I do have to say that  obviously I'm a massive Stargate fan I  absolutely love Brad Wright he was the  showrunner from Stargate sg1 Atlantis  and universe he was involved in every  aspect of Stargate and made it what it  was  perfect television show but Stargate is  now owned by Amazon NGM has been  purchased and for whatever reason Amazon  have decided not to push on with Brad  Wright this does make me sad because in  an Ideal World Brad Wright being  involved would be the ideal solution for  everyone involved the viewers would  absolutely love it because they'd come  back to see the show that they knew and  loved we'd know that this target  franchise was in good hands because it's  literally in the hands of the person  that bought it to us in the beginning  and Amazon can sit there safely in the  knowledge knowing that the new property  that they've just purchased is in safe  hands  but they didn't go for that option  they've obviously decided to press on  with someone else I'm going to be  playing devil's advocate here because  although I do really want Brad Wright to  be involved  is it really that much of an issue if  he's not speaking from my own personal  experiences I have been wanting Stargate  back on my screen ever since Stargate  Universe ended to me Stargate Universe  ended prematurely it was just getting  good and then it was taken away from us  all of the Stargate projects that were  in the works at the time were also  scrapped there was no Stargate  Extinction the Stargate Atlantis movie  there was no Stargate revolutions which  was the next movie for this target sg1  series we never got a third season of  the Target Universe and one of the  bigger projects the Stargate worlds  which was a massively multiplayer online  role-playing game that was scrapped as  well for over a decade I've been wanting  Stargate back in some form and as a fan  who is desperate to see Stargate in some  form I really don't care who brings it  to me when Stargate comes back because I  honestly believe it will  whoever is in charge whoever it may be  I'm going to watch it and I know a lot  of other Stargate fans feel exactly the  same way they're going to watch it  because it's Stargate I use Doctor Who  as an example  um for fantastic science fiction  television shows all of the time and I  always use the reboot as an example for  things like this doctor who went off the  air in the 80s the last doctor to be on  our television screens was Sylvester  McCoy the Seventh Doctor the next time  we saw a doctor who was in Doctor Who  the movie where Sylvester McCoy  regenerated into Paul McGann now after  Doctor Who the movie had ended it was  radio silence for the longest time we  had no Doctor Who  at all it wasn't until 2005 when Russell  T Davis a brand new showrunner took on  Doctor Who and bought it back in a  massive way bringing in Christopher  Eccleston as a Ninth Doctor Who was then  later replaced by David Tennant who is  arguably the most popular doctor of all  time Doctor Who was more popular than it  had ever been and this was under a brand  new showrunner and this is what I want  to compare it to because the possibility  of having Stargate return under a new  showrunner with fresh ideas and a fresh  perspective with new stories of how they  can progress to franchise this new  showrunner could potentially be the  Russell T Davis that we need for  Stargate and it doesn't mean that Brad  Wright won't ever be involved in  Stargate whoever is involved might  actually push for him to get involved in  some way maybe writing a couple of  stories or Consulting on Canon of the  show so when Stargate does return and we  get a new showrunner I'm gonna watch it  because I'm gonna hope  I'm gonna pray and I'm just going to  give it a chance that this new  showrunner whoever is in charge of  Stargate  has a fresh perspective and is going to  make my favorite show  even better let me know what you think  in the comment section down below if you  agree with me let me know and if you  disagree with me leave that in the  comment section down below whilst you're  down there hit subscribe and press the  Bell notification so you don't miss a  single video and also consider becoming  a fully fledged side tracker hit the  join button down below thank you so much  for watching and I will see you next  week  foreign  [Music]
 

